  "summary": "Skills collection bundling third-party install and verify scripts",
  "details": "Package is a collection of bundled 'skills' that includes helper scripts such as bundled-skills/rclone-cli/scripts/install.sh (fetches rclone from https://rclone.org), bundled-skills/youtube-notetaker/scripts/verify.sh (uses curl for GET requests), and Python scraper/API scripts under bundled-skills/junta-leiloeiros/. Rule hits match keyword co-occurrence (curl, ping, GET/POST) in these shipped helper scripts rather than at npm install time. The npm package itself does not declare lifecycle scripts that execute these files on install, and the referenced endpoints (rclone.org) are the official project domains of the tools being wrapped. No credential harvesting, no environment scraping, no hardcoded attacker C2, and no fetch-and-execute of attacker-controlled payloads are present.",
